    },
    {
      "id": "a7b16845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement primarily displays only the lower-division courses required in the major, and a few featured upper-division courses. Although completion of the coursework below is not necessarily mandatory prior to admission, students are strongly advised to complete as much lower division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. This agreement does not contain most upper-division (junior-senior) major requirements, course pre-requisites, general education or all-university coursework necessary for completion of this degree. In some cases, there may be alternative course options at the upper-division level. REFER TO THE FRESNO STATE CATALOG FOR FURTHER INFORMATION: http://www.fresnostate.edu/catalog/",
      "contentHtml": "<p>This agreement primarily displays only the lower-division courses required in the major, and a few featured upper-division courses. Although completion of the coursework below is not necessarily mandatory prior to admission, students are strongly advised to complete as much lower division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. This agreement does not contain most upper-division (junior-senior) major requirements, course pre-requisites, general education or all-university coursework necessary for completion of this degree. In some cases, there may be alternative course options at the upper-division level. REFER TO THE FRESNO STATE CATALOG FOR FURTHER INFORMATION: <a href=\"http://www.fresnostate.edu/catalog/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fresnostate.edu/catalog/</a></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "d9b76845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "General Information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e0b76845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "NOTE: NEW MAJORS IN AUDIOLOGY ARE SUSPENDED UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE. The Bachelor of Arts degree in Communicative Sciences provides the students with a liberal arts foundation integrated with courses designed to provide a basic understanding of speech, language, and hearing development and communicative problems. Audiology is a career path that is exciting and growing everyday. With the new advancements in medical technology more and more is known about the human ear. Audiologists are primarily concerned with the hearing system of the ear as well as balance of the body. Experts in the field are also concerned with prevention of hearing loss, identification and treatment of hearing and balance systems, and rehabilitation of persons with hearing and balance problems. If you are interested in this field, the first step is to acquire a bachelor's degree and a AuD (Doctor of Audiology) degree. Coursework includes basic science, math, auditory systems and abnormal communication development. Those with graduate degrees must obtain a certificate of clinical competence (CCC) from the American Speech Hearing and Language Association (ASHA) and then apply for a license to practice. Every state is different in their licensure practices. Advising Notes CR/NC grading is not permitted for CSDS majors for any coursework required in the major, with the exception of clinical courses. Students in clinical, internship, and student teaching courses are required to show health certification that they are free from tuberculosis and rubella, and to purchase student clinic malpractice insurance for the clinical courses (see the University Speech and Hearing Clinic director for details). In addition to the major program requirements, every student must also complete the University’s baccalaureate degree requirements such as: American Government and Institutions ( PLSI 2 ) General Education Requirements (43 units) Additional University Graduation Requirements (9 units) Upper-Division Writing Requirement General Education, Additional University Graduation Requirements, and Upper-division Writing courses can be double counted with major requirements. See advisor for details. Sufficient Elective Units to Meet Required Total Units (varies); it is recommended that units in this area be utilized to complete a second major or minor. See advising notes 4 and 5 for recommended electives. A full description of the University’s graduation requirements can be found in the Baccalaureate Degree Requirements .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><u>NOTE:&nbsp;</u></strong><u style=\"font-size: 16px;\">NEW MAJORS IN AUDIOLOGY ARE SUSPENDED UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE.</u></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The Bachelor of Arts degree in Communicative Sciences provides the students with a liberal arts foundation integrated with courses designed to provide a basic understanding of speech, language, and hearing development and communicative problems.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Audiology is a career path that is exciting and growing everyday. With the new advancements in medical technology more and more is known about the human ear. Audiologists are primarily concerned with the hearing system of the ear as well as balance of the body. Experts in the field are also concerned with prevention of hearing loss, identification and treatment of hearing and balance systems, and rehabilitation of persons with hearing and balance problems.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">If you are interested in this field, the first step is to acquire a bachelor's degree and a AuD (Doctor of Audiology) degree. Coursework includes basic science, math, auditory systems and abnormal communication development. Those with graduate degrees must obtain a certificate of clinical competence (CCC) from the American Speech Hearing and Language Association (ASHA) and then apply for a license to practice. Every state is different in their licensure practices.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Advising Notes</strong></p><p class=\"highlight\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">CR/NC grading is not permitted for CSDS majors for any coursework required in the major, with the exception of clinical courses.</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Students in clinical, internship, and student teaching courses are required to show health certification that they are free from tuberculosis and rubella, and to purchase student clinic malpractice insurance for the clinical courses (see the University Speech and Hearing Clinic director for details).</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">In addition to the major program requirements, every student must also complete the University’s baccalaureate degree requirements such as:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">American Government and Institutions (</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3174&amp;returnto=230#tt8749\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">PLSI 2</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">)</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=249\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General Education</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;Requirements (43&nbsp;units)</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Additional University Graduation Requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(9 units)</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=245\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Upper-Division Writing</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;Requirement</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General Education, Additional University Graduation Requirements, and Upper-division Writing courses can be double counted with major requirements. See advisor for details.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Sufficient Elective Units to Meet Required Total Units (varies); it is recommended that units in this area be utilized to complete a second major or minor.&nbsp;See advising notes 4 and 5 for recommended electives.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">A full description of the University’s graduation requirements can be found in the Baccalaureate&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=234\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Degree Requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">.</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "639b0a24-a602-44d6-9d2f-01982e92b4a8",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Additional University Graduation Requirements The Additional University Graduation Requirements are designed to complement the GE requirements. It is the policy of Fresno State, that all students will cultivate and refine their affective, cognitive, and physical faculties through studying great works of the human imagination; be equipped for lifelong understanding and development of themselves as integrated physiological, social, and psychological beings; and be prepared to understand and live in a multicultural and international world through their undergraduate education. This will be accomplished through a total of 9 units from the following areas, each requiring 3 units: Arts/Humanities (A/H) - All students are required to take an Arts/Humanities course to graduate at the bachelor’s degree level. Lifelong-Understanding and Self-Development (L/S) - All students are required to take a lifelong understanding and self-development course to for graduate at the bachelor’s degree level. Multicultural/International (M/I) - All Students are required to take a Multicultural / International course at Fresno State to graduate at the bachelor’s degree level.",
      "contentHtml": "<h1>Additional University Graduation Requirements</h1><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The&nbsp;Additional University Graduation Requirements are designed to complement the GE requirements. It is the policy of Fresno State, that all students will cultivate and refine their affective, cognitive, and physical faculties through studying great works of the human imagination; be equipped for lifelong understanding and development of themselves as integrated physiological, social, and psychological beings; and be prepared to understand and live in a multicultural and international world through their undergraduate education.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This will be accomplished through a total of 9 units from the following areas, each requiring 3 units:</span></p><ol><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#ah\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Arts/Humanities (A/H)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All students are required to take an Arts/Humanities&nbsp;course to graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#ls\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Lifelong-Understanding and Self-Development (L/S)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All students are required to take a lifelong understanding and self-development course to&nbsp;for graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#mi\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Multicultural/International (M/I)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All Students are required to take a Multicultural / International course at Fresno State to graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
